    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "subjective",
      "section": "Section D",
      "marks": 5,
      "question": "Find the derivative of $f(x) = x^2$ from first principles.",
      "finalAnswer": "$2x$",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "$f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h}$.",
        "$= \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{(x+h)^2 - x^2}{h}$.",
        "$= \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{x^2 + 2xh + h^2 - x^2}{h}$.",
        "$= \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{h(2x+h)}{h}$.",
        "$= \\lim_{h \\to 0} (2x+h) = 2x$."
      ]
    },
